{:edb/committed true :edb/basis-t 1190 :edb/replayed false :edb/tx-hash "23586f1a3d46ff4bc54df88a60fa566bfe9c23f6f1a1e9e1674f7eb7ba7321f5" :edb/db-before-t 1189 :edb/db-after-t 1190 :edb/tx-data [[13194139534502 50 #inst "2026-10-07T18:27:10.059Z" 13194139534502 true] [17592186175707 1100 "A particle $P$ moves along the $x$-axis and its velocity at time $t$ is given by $v(t) = 2t + 3t^2$. What is the total displacement of the particle between $t=1$ and $t=3$?" 13194139534502 false] [17592186175707 1100 "A particle $P$ moves along the $x$-axis and its velocity at time $t$ is given by $v(t) = 2t + 3t^2.$ What is the total displacement of the particle between $t=1$ and $t=3?$" 13194139534502 true] [17592186175707 1145 "We find the total displacement by calculating the definite integral of the velocity.\n\nLet $d$ be the total displacement. Then, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nd &= ∫_{1}^{3}(2t + 3t^{2})dt \\\\\n&= (t^{2} + t^{3}) \\mid _{1}^{3} \\\\\n&= [3^{2} + 3^{3}] - [1^{2} + 1^{3}] \\\\\n&= [9 + 27] - [1 + 1] \\\\\n&= 36 - 2 \\\\\n&= 34\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo the total displacement between $t=1$ and $t=3$ is $34$." 13194139534502 false] [17592186175707 1145 "We find the total displacement by calculating the definite integral of the velocity.\n\nLet $d$ be the total displacement. Then, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}d & ={\\int }_{1}^{3}(2t+3{t}^{2})\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={({t}^{2}+{t}^{3})|}_{1}^{3} \\\\  & =[{3}^{2}+{3}^{3}]-[{1}^{2}+{1}^{3}] \\\\  & =[9+27]-[1+1] \\\\  & =36-2 \\\\  & =34.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo the total displacement between $t=1$ and $t=3$ is $34.$" 13194139534502 true] [17592186175719 1100 "A particle $P$ moves along the $x$-axis and its velocity at time $t>0$ is given by $v(t) = 6t^2 +4t$. At time $t=2$ the particle is located at the position $x=-20$. What is the position of the particle at time $t=4$?" 13194139534502 false] [17592186175719 1100 "A particle $P$ moves along the $x$-axis and its velocity at time $t>0$ is given by $v(t) = 6t^2 +4t.$ At time $t=2$ the particle is located at the position $x=-20.$ What is the position of the particle at time $t=4?$" 13194139534502 true] [17592186175719 1145 "The position of the particle at $t=4$ is equal to its position at $t=2$ plus the total displacement over $t\\in[2,4]$. Therefore, we can calculate it as follows:\n\n$$\nx(4) = x(2) + \\int_2^4 v(t)\\,\\textrm{d}t\n$$\n\nCarrying out the computations, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nx(4) &= -20 + ∫_{2}^{4}(6t^{2} + 4t)dt \\\\\n&=-20 + [2t^{3} + 2t^{2}]_{2}^{4} \\\\\n&=-20 + ([2(4)^{3} + 2(4)^{2}] - [2(2)^{3} + 2(2)^{2}]) \\\\\n&=-20 + ([128 + 32] - [16 + 8]) \\\\\n&=-20 + (160 - 24) \\\\\n&=-20 + 136 \\\\\n&= 116\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo the position of the particle at $t=4$ is $x=116$." 13194139534502 false] [17592186175719 1145 "The position of the particle at $t=4$ is equal to its position at $t=2$ plus the total displacement over $t\\in[2,4].$ Therefore, we can calculate it as follows:\n\n$$\nx(4) = x(2) + \\int_2^4 v(t)\\,\\textrm{d}t\n$$\n\nCarrying out the computations, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(4) & =-20+{\\int }_{2}^{4}(6{t}^{2}+4t)\\,\\text{dt} \\\\  & =-20+{[2{t}^{3}+2{t}^{2}]}_{2}^{4} \\\\  & =-20+([2(4)^{3}+2(4)^{2}]-[2(2)^{3}+2(2)^{2}]) \\\\  & =-20+([128+32]-[16+8]) \\\\  & =-20+(160-24) \\\\  & =-20+136 \\\\  & =116.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo the position of the particle at $t=4$ is $x=116.$" 13194139534502 true] [17592186175720 1100 "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14014400/assets/900988cb8ec54abcafc256a34c685829d2f5f00cdca373ad84dfa0ef70cc3957.png)\n\nThe graph above shows the velocity of an object moving in a straight line along the $x$-axis. At time $t=2$ the particle is located at the position $x=-1.$ What is the position of the particle at time $t=8?$" 13194139534502 true] [17592186175720 1100 "The graph above shows the velocity of an object moving in a straight line along the $x$-axis. At time $t=2$ the particle is located at the position $x=-1$. What is the position of the particle at time $t=8$?\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/MA/DATA/Lessons/3576/Source/Images/1e5634171531dd04f9da7173af00e15c.png)" 13194139534502 false] [17592186175720 1145 "The position of the particle at $t = 8$ is equal to its position at $t=2$ plus the total displacement over $t\\in [2,8]$. Therefore, we can calculate it as follows:\n\n$$\nx(8) = x(2)+ \\int_2^8 v(t) \\, \\textrm d t\n$$\n\nWe are told that $x(2)=-1$, and we can compute the integral $\\displaystyle\\int_2^8 v(t) \\, \\textrm dt$ by finding the signed area under the graph from $t=2$ to $t=8$. Computing the signed area, we get\n\n$$\n\\int_2^8 v(t) \\, \\textrm dt = 6\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\nx(8) = -1+ 6 = 5\n$$\n\nSo the position of the particle at $t=8$ is $x=5$." 13194139534502 false] [17592186175720 1145 "The position of the particle at $t = 8$ is equal to its position at $t=2$ plus the total displacement over $t\\in [2,8].$ Therefore, we can calculate it as follows:\n\n$$\nx(8) = x(2)+ \\int_2^8 v(t) \\, \\textrm d t\n$$\n\nWe are told that $x(2)=-1$, and we can compute the integral $\\displaystyle\\int_2^8 v(t) \\, \\textrm dt$ by finding the signed area under the graph from $t=2$ to $t=8.$ Computing the signed area, we get\n\n$$\n\\int_2^8 v(t) \\, \\textrm dt = 6.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\nx(8) = -1+ 6 = 5\n$$\n\nSo the position of the particle at $t=8$ is $x=5.$" 13194139534502 true] [17592186175851 1020 #edb/ref 17592186292152 13194139534502 true] [17592186175851 1020 #edb/ref 17592186292180 13194139534502 true] [17592186175851 1020 #edb/ref 17592186292191 13194139534502 true] [17592186175851 1020 #edb/ref 17592186292194 13194139534502 true] [17592186175851 1020 #edb/ref 17592186292198 13194139534502 true] [17592186175876 1020 #edb/ref 17592186292159 13194139534502 true] [17592186175876 1020 #edb/ref 17592186292166 13194139534502 true] [17592186175876 1020 #edb/ref 17592186292173 13194139534502 true] [17592186175876 1020 #edb/ref 17592186292202 13194139534502 true] [17592186175876 1020 #edb/ref 17592186292214 13194139534502 true] [17592186175877 1020 #edb/ref 17592186292187 13194139534502 true] [17592186175877 1020 #edb/ref 17592186292205 13194139534502 true] [17592186175877 1020 #edb/ref 17592186292208 13194139534502 true] [17592186175877 1020 #edb/ref 17592186292211 13194139534502 true] [17592186175877 1020 #edb/ref 17592186292221 13194139534502 true] [17592186292152 1017 #edb/ref 17592186292153 13194139534502 true] [17592186292152 1089 "q-120986" 13194139534502 true] [17592186292152 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139534502 true] [17592186292152 1100 "A particle $P$ moves along the $x$-axis and its velocity at time $t$ is given by $v(t)=6{t}^{2}+t-\\frac{3}{2}.$ What is the total displacement of the particle between $t=1$ and $t=4?$" 13194139534502 true] [17592186292152 1113 #uuid "1db46de8-934a-56e6-8549-c49709f0e59b" 13194139534502 true] [17592186292152 1145 "We find the total displacement by calculating the definite integral of the velocity.\n\nLet $d$ be the total displacement. Then we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}d & ={\\int }_{1}^{4}(6{t}^{2}+t-\\frac{3}{2})\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={(2{t}^{3}+\\frac{1}{2}{t}^{2}-\\frac{3}{2}t)|}_{1}^{4} \\\\  & =[2(4)^{3}+\\frac{1}{2}(4)^{2}-\\frac{3}{2}(4)]-[2(1)^{3}+\\frac{1}{2}(1)^{2}-\\frac{3}{2}(1)] \\\\  & =[128+8-6]-[2+\\frac{1}{2}-\\frac{3}{2}] \\\\  & =130-1 \\\\  & =129.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo the total displacement between $t=1$ and $t=4$ is $129.$" 13194139534502 true] [17592186292153 1000 #edb/ref 17592186292154 13194139534502 true] [17592186292153 1000 #edb/ref 17592186292155 13194139534502 true] [17592186292153 1000 #edb/ref 17592186292156 13194139534502 true] [17592186292153 1000 #edb/ref 17592186292157 13194139534502 true] [17592186292153 1000 #edb/ref 17592186292158 13194139534502 true] [17592186292153 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534502 true] [17592186292153 1041 "selection" 13194139534502 true] [17592186292153 1104 #edb/ref 17592186292156 13194139534502 true] [17592186292153 1110 #uuid "42c84250-2608-5f3a-a98b-b53e6e7aec7f" 13194139534502 true] [17592186292154 1034 "130" 13194139534502 true] [17592186292154 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534502 true] [17592186292154 1111 #uuid "92a5264e-7d94-5c1d-a759-d572d6b86fb4" 13194139534502 true] [17592186292155 1034 "128" 13194139534502 true] [17592186292155 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534502 true] [17592186292155 1111 #uuid "0343c5ae-1864-5196-a573-9139e23d2dcf" 13194139534502 true] [17592186292156 1034 "129" 13194139534502 true] [17592186292156 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534502 true] [17592186292156 1111 #uuid "bfa31d4f-88e5-5fa5-a681-012e44d672fe" 13194139534502 true] [17592186292157 1034 "127" 13194139534502 true] [17592186292157 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534502 true] [17592186292157 1111 #uuid "142ef266-14ba-56f6-a9bf-0f405ca6d929" 13194139534502 true] [17592186292158 1034 "131" 13194139534502 true] [17592186292158 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534502 true] [17592186292158 1111 #uuid "8ff009f7-6fe4-5510-9b6f-21a8925e221d" 13194139534502 true] [17592186292159 1017 #edb/ref 17592186292160 13194139534502 true] [17592186292159 1089 "q-120998" 13194139534502 true] [17592186292159 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045464 13194139534502 true] [17592186292159 1100 "A particle $P$ moves along the $x$-axis and its velocity at time $t>0$ is given by $v(t)={e}^{2t+1}.$ At time $t=0.5$ the particle is located at the position $x={e}^{2}.$ What is the position of the particle at time $t=2?$" 13194139534502 true] [17592186292159 1113 #uuid "b71dab59-3f02-59fd-8bdb-cc10afd7de9b" 13194139534502 true] [17592186292159 1145 "The position of the particle at $t=2$ is equal to its position at $t=0.5$ plus the total displacement over $t\\in [0.5,2].$ Therefore, we can calculate it as follows:\n\n$$\nx(2)=x(0.5)+{\\int }_{0.5}^{2}v(t)\\,\\text{d}t\n$$\n\nCarrying out the computations, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(2) & ={e}^{2}+{\\int }_{0.5}^{2}{e}^{2t+1}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={e}^{2}+{[\\frac{1}{2}{e}^{2t+1}]}_{0.5}^{2} \\\\  & ={e}^{2}+(\\frac{1}{2}{e}^{2(2)+1}-\\frac{1}{2}{e}^{2(0.5)+1}) \\\\  & ={e}^{2}+(\\frac{1}{2}{e}^{5}-\\frac{1}{2}{e}^{2}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}{e}^{2}+\\frac{1}{2}{e}^{5} \\\\  & =\\frac{{e}^{2}+{e}^{5}}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the position of the particle at $t=2$ is $x=\\frac{{e}^{2}+{e}^{5}}{2}.$" 13194139534502 true] [17592186292160 1000 #edb/ref 17592186292161 13194139534502 true] [17592186292160 1000 #edb/ref 17592186292162 13194139534502 true] [17592186292160 1000 #edb/ref 17592186292163 13194139534502 true] [17592186292160 1000 #edb/ref 17592186292164 13194139534502 true] [17592186292160 1000 #edb/ref 17592186292165 13194139534502 true] [17592186292160 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534502 true] [17592186292160 1041 "selection" 13194139534502 true] [17592186292160 1104 #edb/ref 17592186292161 13194139534502 true] [17592186292160 1110 #uuid "dceeeff9-88af-5a13-b08e-b51205cce197" 13194139534502 true] [17592186292161 1034 "\\frac{{e}^{2}+{e}^{5}}{2}" 13194139534502 true] [17592186292161 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534502 true] [17592186292161 1111 #uuid "6bd0dc61-87e5-5c07-a8ad-7609bcfb4a04" 13194139534502 true] [17592186292162 1034 "{e}^{5}" 13194139534502 true] [17592186292162 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534502 true] [17592186292162 1111 #uuid "8b2ba7c0-c86b-5233-bf50-b8c40aafc11b" 13194139534502 true] [17592186292163 1034 "{e}^{2}+{e}^{5}" 13194139534502 true] [17592186292163 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534502 true] [17592186292163 1111 #uuid "97a307c9-ca06-58b0-b859-571f48287258" 13194139534502 true] [17592186292164 1034 "\\frac{{e}^{5}}{2}" 13194139534502 true] [17592186292164 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534502 true] [17592186292164 1111 #uuid "3958d845-9630-5738-a448-0eb61ee51e89" 13194139534502 true] [17592186292165 1034 "\\frac{{e}^{2}}{2}" 13194139534502 true] [17592186292165 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534502 true] [17592186292165 1111 #uuid "32f21e3a-1993-56f1-9adc-31ba974e5450" 13194139534502 true] [17592186292166 1017 #edb/ref 17592186292167 13194139534502 true] [17592186292166 1089 "q-121000" 13194139534502 true] [17592186292166 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045464 13194139534502 true] [17592186292166 1100 "A particle $P$ moves along the $x$-axis and its velocity at time $t>0$ is given by $v(t)=3{e}^{3t-1}.$ At time $t=1$ the particle is located at the position $x=2{e}^{2}.$ What is the position of the particle at time $t=5?$" 13194139534502 true] [17592186292166 1113 #uuid "d7d90ca4-6723-5cb8-bec5-48fa186d8bab" 13194139534502 true] [17592186292166 1145 "The position of the particle at $t=5$ is equal to its position at $t=1$ plus the total displacement over $t\\in [1,5].$ Therefore, we can calculate it as follows:\n\n$$\nx(5)=x(1)+{\\int }_{1}^{5}v(t)\\,\\text{d}t\n$$\n\nCarrying out the computations, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(5) & =2{e}^{2}+{\\int }_{1}^{5}3{e}^{3t-1}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =2{e}^{2}+{[{e}^{3t-1}]}_{1}^{5} \\\\  & =2{e}^{2}+({e}^{3(5)-1}-{e}^{3(1)-1}) \\\\  & =2{e}^{2}+({e}^{14}-{e}^{2}) \\\\  & =2{e}^{2}+{e}^{14}-{e}^{2} \\\\  & ={e}^{2}+{e}^{14}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the position of the particle at $t=5$ is $x={e}^{2}+{e}^{14}.$" 13194139534502 true] [17592186292167 1000 #edb/ref 17592186292168 13194139534502 true] [17592186292167 1000 #edb/ref 17592186292169 13194139534502 true] [17592186292167 1000 #edb/ref 17592186292170 13194139534502 true] [17592186292167 1000 #edb/ref 17592186292171 13194139534502 true] [17592186292167 1000 #edb/ref 17592186292172 13194139534502 true] [17592186292167 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534502 true] [17592186292167 1041 "selection" 13194139534502 true] [17592186292167 1104 #edb/ref 17592186292172 13194139534502 true] [17592186292167 1110 #uuid "d1ee0a4b-fcac-5fe8-9f33-bc672bd54359" 13194139534502 true] [17592186292168 1034 "{e}^{14}-{e}^{2}+1" 13194139534502 true] [17592186292168 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534502 true] [17592186292168 1111 #uuid "cdbe0437-44c0-53c4-ab8c-e387e22a1e97" 13194139534502 true] [17592186292169 1034 "3{e}^{2}+{e}^{14}" 13194139534502 true] [17592186292169 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534502 true] [17592186292169 1111 #uuid "ddf3911c-cd3c-5139-b3e9-a42a8efaa35d" 13194139534502 true] [17592186292170 1034 "{e}^{2}+{e}^{16}" 13194139534502 true] [17592186292170 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534502 true] [17592186292170 1111 #uuid "9267816a-01c3-543b-8f34-03bf72c8177c" 13194139534502 true] [17592186292171 1034 "{e}^{16}-{e}^{2}+1" 13194139534502 true] [17592186292171 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534502 true] [17592186292171 1111 #uuid "74fa6180-72ce-544e-a360-9d65bcf920d0" 13194139534502 true] [17592186292172 1034 "{e}^{2}+{e}^{14}" 13194139534502 true] [17592186292172 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534502 true] [17592186292172 1111 #uuid "db6b02a4-0d65-5140-b97d-2835c713ce2f" 13194139534502 true] [17592186292173 1017 #edb/ref 17592186292174 13194139534502 true] [17592186292173 1089 "q-121007" 13194139534502 true] [17592186292173 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045464 13194139534502 true] [17592186292173 1100 "A particle $P$ moves along the $x$-axis and its velocity at time $t\\ge 0$ is given by $v(t)=\\operatorname{sin}⁡(t-\\frac{\\pi }{3}).$ At time $t=\\frac{\\pi }{3}$ the particle is located at the position $x=\\frac{1}{2}.$ What is the position of the particle at time $t=\\pi ?$" 13194139534502 true] [17592186292173 1113 #uuid "c1052200-d76a-59c5-989a-4d2d76d89a0b" 13194139534502 true] [17592186292173 1145 "The position of the particle at $t=\\pi $ is equal to its position at $t=\\frac{\\pi }{3}$ plus the total displacement over $t\\in [\\frac{\\pi }{3},\\pi ].$ Therefore, we can calculate it as follows:\n\n$$\nx(\\pi )=x(\\frac{\\pi }{3})+{\\int }_{\\pi /3}^{\\pi }v(t)\\,\\text{d}t\n$$\n\nCarrying out the computations, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(\\pi ) & =\\frac{1}{2}+{\\int }_{\\pi /3}^{\\pi }\\operatorname{sin}⁡(t-\\frac{\\pi }{3})\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}+{[-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(t-\\frac{\\pi }{3})]}_{\\pi /3}^{\\pi } \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}+([-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\pi -\\frac{\\pi }{3})]-[-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{3}-\\frac{\\pi }{3})]) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}+(-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{2\\pi }{3})+\\operatorname{cos}⁡(0)) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}+(-(-\\frac{1}{2})+1) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}+\\frac{1}{2}+1 \\\\  & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the position of the particle at $t=\\pi $ is $x=2.$" 13194139534502 true] [17592186292174 1000 #edb/ref 17592186292175 13194139534502 true] [17592186292174 1000 #edb/ref 17592186292176 13194139534502 true] [17592186292174 1000 #edb/ref 17592186292177 13194139534502 true] [17592186292174 1000 #edb/ref 17592186292178 13194139534502 true] [17592186292174 1000 #edb/ref 17592186292179 13194139534502 true] [17592186292174 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534502 true] [17592186292174 1041 "selection" 13194139534502 true] [17592186292174 1104 #edb/ref 17592186292177 13194139534502 true] [17592186292174 1110 #uuid "cea03fbc-b338-53c9-a25a-30131b5aa091" 13194139534502 true] [17592186292175 1034 "\\frac{\\pi }{3}+\\frac{3}{2}" 13194139534502 true] [17592186292175 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534502 true] [17592186292175 1111 #uuid "eb5b1566-17c3-58b8-b00f-6cda1cf93271" 13194139534502 true] [17592186292176 1034 "\\frac{1}{2}" 13194139534502 true] [17592186292176 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534502 true] [17592186292176 1111 #uuid "fdb5ec3c-ac4f-533f-81f2-1fdb1ed88d23" 13194139534502 true] [17592186292177 1034 "2" 13194139534502 true] [17592186292177 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534502 true] [17592186292177 1111 #uuid "5332815c-36c3-58d9-991f-722f4ba2c53d" 13194139534502 true] [17592186292178 1034 "1" 13194139534502 true] [17592186292178 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534502 true] [17592186292178 1111 #uuid "3e1036c0-52e5-5d1c-8c38-60f8e5543902" 13194139534502 true] [17592186292179 1034 "\\frac{3}{2}" 13194139534502 true] [17592186292179 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534502 true] [17592186292179 1111 #uuid "92a786cd-fd48-5d59-bc9a-24358582507e" 13194139534502 true] [17592186292180 1017 #edb/ref 17592186292181 13194139534502 true] [17592186292180 1089 "q-19494" 13194139534502 true] [17592186292180 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139534502 true] [17592186292180 1100 "A particle $P$ moves along the $x$-axis and its velocity at time $t$ is given by $v(t)={t}^{2}-7t+10.$ What is the total displacement of the particle between $t=2$ and $t=5?$" 13194139534502 true] [17592186292180 1113 #uuid "16ed4b22-8600-5440-b196-0307bbc3ead4" 13194139534502 true] [17592186292180 1145 "We find the total displacement by calculating the definite integral of the velocity.\n\nLet $d$ be the total displacement. Then we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}d & ={\\int }_{2}^{5}({t}^{2}-7t+10)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={(\\frac{1}{3}{t}^{3}-\\frac{7}{2}{t}^{2}+10t)|}_{2}^{5} \\\\  & =[\\frac{1}{3}(5)^{3}-\\frac{7}{2}(5)^{2}+10(5)]-[\\frac{1}{3}(2)^{3}-\\frac{7}{2}(2)^{2}+10(2)] \\\\  & =[\\frac{125}{3}-\\frac{175}{2}+50]-[\\frac{8}{3}-14+20] \\\\  & =\\frac{25}{6}-\\frac{26}{3} \\\\  & =-\\frac{9}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nSo the total displacement between $t=2$ and $t=5$ is $-\\frac{9}{2}.$" 13194139534502 true] [17592186292181 1000 #edb/ref 17592186292182 13194139534502 true] [17592186292181 1000 #edb/ref 17592186292183 13194139534502 true] [17592186292181 1000 #edb/ref 17592186292184 13194139534502 true] [17592186292181 1000 #edb/ref 17592186292185 13194139534502 true] [17592186292181 1000 #edb/ref 17592186292186 13194139534502 true] [17592186292181 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534502 true] [17592186292181 1041 "selection" 13194139534502 true] [17592186292181 1104 #edb/ref 17592186292184 13194139534502 true] [17592186292181 1110 #uuid "24347589-3e14-56df-ba32-c36cc5aeef99" 13194139534502 true] [17592186292182 1034 "-\\frac{25}{6}" 13194139534502 true] [17592186292182 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534502 true] [17592186292182 1111 #uuid "611264e7-e158-5b06-9f19-145b4c39ebd5" 13194139534502 true] [17592186292183 1034 "\\frac{27}{5}" 13194139534502 true] [17592186292183 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534502 true] [17592186292183 1111 #uuid "60f963c3-cba3-5aa8-a8eb-7aaa60fc9c16" 13194139534502 true] [17592186292184 1034 "-\\frac{9}{2}" 13194139534502 true] [17592186292184 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534502 true] [17592186292184 1111 #uuid "db895c28-d357-541c-b966-7cebcb85a7ab" 13194139534502 true] [17592186292185 1034 "\\frac{25}{3}" 13194139534502 true] [17592186292185 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534502 true] [17592186292185 1111 #uuid "a5293353-e707-5799-9b04-10f5c8d371ba" 13194139534502 true] [17592186292186 1034 "-\\frac{26}{3}" 13194139534502 true] [17592186292186 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534502 true] [17592186292186 1111 #uuid "810edcee-4228-5be6-ad8c-8ed3ad11d644" 13194139534502 true] [17592186292187 1017 #edb/ref 17592186292188 13194139534502 true] [17592186292187 1089 "q-348321" 13194139534502 true] [17592186292187 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139534502 true] [17592186292187 1100 "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14014400/assets/e51b807bc238b140215a8a753fcfe778b14735e723dd5cb43b8aab22039a8e8e.png)\n\nThe graph above shows the velocity of an object moving in a straight line along the $x$-axis. At time $t=0,$ the particle is located at the position $x=-2.$ What is the position of the particle at time $t=4?$\n\nThe position of the particle at $t=4$ is $x=$\n{{field-1}}." 13194139534502 true] [17592186292187 1113 #uuid "2c89b745-0982-5313-bdde-182c5954d58e" 13194139534502 true] [17592186292187 1145 "The position of the particle at $t=4$ is equal to its position at $t=0$ plus the total displacement over $t\\in [0,4].$ Therefore, we can calculate it as follows:\n\n$$\nx(4)=x(0)+{\\int }_{0}^{4}v(t)\\,\\text{d}t\n$$\n\nWe are told that $x(0)=-2$, and we can compute the integral ${\\int }_{0}^{4}v(t)\\,\\text{d}t$ by finding the signed area under the graph from $t=0$ to $t=4.$ Computing the signed area, we get\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{0}^{4}v(t)\\,\\text{d}t=12.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\nx(4)=-2+12=10.\n$$\n\nSo the position of the particle at $t=4$ is $x=10.$" 13194139534502 true] [17592186292188 1000 #edb/ref 17592186292189 13194139534502 true] [17592186292188 1000 #edb/ref 17592186292190 13194139534502 true] [17592186292188 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139534502 true] [17592186292188 1041 "field-1" 13194139534502 true] [17592186292188 1104 #edb/ref 17592186292190 13194139534502 true] [17592186292188 1110 #uuid "07e26a32-524b-516d-b2d3-3acb9bd5f749" 13194139534502 true] [17592186292189 1034 "12" 13194139534502 true] [17592186292189 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534502 true] [17592186292189 1111 #uuid "83a6f011-1d09-56e7-a775-9ab675b9e15d" 13194139534502 true] [17592186292190 1034 "10" 13194139534502 true] [17592186292190 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534502 true] [17592186292190 1111 #uuid "890b7b85-ee59-546f-a0f6-e52a7a51dab7" 13194139534502 true] [17592186292191 1017 #edb/ref 17592186292192 13194139534502 true] [17592186292191 1089 "q-351421" 13194139534502 true] [17592186292191 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139534502 true] [17592186292191 1100 "A particle $Q$ moves along the $x$-axis and its velocity at time $t$ is given by $v(t)=6t+2.$ Find the total displacement $d$ of the particle between $t=1$ and $t=2.$\n\n$d=$\n{{field-1}}" 13194139534502 true] [17592186292191 1113 #uuid "0bc88c45-b00a-5e19-9c3f-9d3e4f3af636" 13194139534502 true] [17592186292191 1145 "We find the total displacement by calculating the definite integral of the velocity.\n\nLet $d$ be the total displacement between $t=1$ and $t=2.$ Then we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}d & ={\\int }_{1}^{2}(6t+2)\\,\\text{dt} \\\\  & =(3{t}^{2}+2t){|}_{1}^{2} \\\\  & =[3(2)^{2}+2(2)]-[3(1)^{2}+2(1)] \\\\  & =[12+4]-[3+2] \\\\  & =11.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534502 true] [17592186292192 1000 #edb/ref 17592186292193 13194139534502 true] [17592186292192 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139534502 true] [17592186292192 1041 "field-1" 13194139534502 true] [17592186292192 1104 #edb/ref 17592186292193 13194139534502 true] [17592186292192 1110 #uuid "9d45bbc9-97c0-5571-9e73-7d150a54b469" 13194139534502 true] [17592186292193 1034 "11" 13194139534502 true] [17592186292193 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534502 true] [17592186292193 1111 #uuid "f41b1b34-f997-5d61-9acc-0574bcd388cf" 13194139534502 true] [17592186292194 1017 #edb/ref 17592186292195 13194139534502 true] [17592186292194 1089 "q-351430" 13194139534502 true] [17592186292194 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139534502 true] [17592186292194 1100 "A particle $Q$ moves along the $x$-axis and its velocity at time $t$ is given by $v(t)=16-9{t}^{2}.$ Find the total displacement $d$ of the particle between $t=3$ and $t=4.$\n\n$d=$\n{{field-1}}" 13194139534502 true] [17592186292194 1113 #uuid "6e25066f-b114-5d4b-8ff9-3e93d1808c46" 13194139534502 true] [17592186292194 1145 "We find the total displacement by calculating the definite integral of the velocity.\n\nLet $d$ be the total displacement between $t=3$ and $t=4.$ Then we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}d & ={\\int }_{3}^{4}(16-9{t}^{2})\\,\\text{dt} \\\\  & ={(16t-3{t}^{3})|}_{3}^{4} \\\\  & =[16(4)-3(4)^{3}]-[16(3)-3(3)^{3}] \\\\  & =[64-192]-[48-81] \\\\  & =-95.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534502 true] [17592186292195 1000 #edb/ref 17592186292196 13194139534502 true] [17592186292195 1000 #edb/ref 17592186292197 13194139534502 true] [17592186292195 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139534502 true] [17592186292195 1041 "field-1" 13194139534502 true] [17592186292195 1104 #edb/ref 17592186292196 13194139534502 true] [17592186292195 1110 #uuid "b55e316f-3bbb-59bb-987e-a56715861c55" 13194139534502 true] [17592186292196 1034 "-95" 13194139534502 true] [17592186292196 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534502 true] [17592186292196 1111 #uuid "f5f22ce7-e843-5b2f-aa76-d8a89bec012d" 13194139534502 true] [17592186292197 1034 "95" 13194139534502 true] [17592186292197 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534502 true] [17592186292197 1111 #uuid "82e94eae-a41e-526d-9760-a60a7c5b5740" 13194139534502 true] [17592186292198 1017 #edb/ref 17592186292199 13194139534502 true] [17592186292198 1089 "q-351431" 13194139534502 true] [17592186292198 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139534502 true] [17592186292198 1100 "A particle $Q$ moves along the $x$-axis and its velocity at time $t$ is given by $v(t)=\\frac{3}{2}\\sqrt{t-1}.$ Find the total displacement $d$ of the particle between $t=1$ and $t=5.$ Do not round the answer.\n\n$d=$\n{{field-1}}" 13194139534502 true] [17592186292198 1113 #uuid "b821d35a-eba2-5209-a10b-30b5c53aa6ef" 13194139534502 true] [17592186292198 1145 "We find the total displacement by calculating the definite integral of the velocity.\n\nLet $d$ be the total displacement between $t=1$ and $t=5.$ Then we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}d & ={\\int }_{1}^{5}(\\frac{3}{2}\\sqrt{t-1})\\,\\text{dt} \\\\  & =(t-1)^{3/2}\\,{|}_{1}^{5} \\\\  & =(5-1)^{3/2}-(1-1)^{3/2} \\\\  & =8-0 \\\\  & =8.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534502 true] [17592186292199 1000 #edb/ref 17592186292200 13194139534502 true] [17592186292199 1000 #edb/ref 17592186292201 13194139534502 true] [17592186292199 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139534502 true] [17592186292199 1041 "field-1" 13194139534502 true] [17592186292199 1104 #edb/ref 17592186292200 13194139534502 true] [17592186292199 1110 #uuid "e7388b20-851e-58e2-85f6-179c4c96a52c" 13194139534502 true] [17592186292200 1034 "8" 13194139534502 true] [17592186292200 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534502 true] [17592186292200 1111 #uuid "5f0c57e2-a924-5441-b0e9-63ee697c5134" 13194139534502 true] [17592186292201 1034 "6" 13194139534502 true] [17592186292201 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534502 true] [17592186292201 1111 #uuid "e5aee0df-8a58-552d-8045-3f53a3f9792d" 13194139534502 true] [17592186292202 1017 #edb/ref 17592186292203 13194139534502 true] [17592186292202 1089 "q-351444" 13194139534502 true] [17592186292202 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045464 13194139534502 true] [17592186292202 1100 "A particle $Q$ moves along the $x$-axis and its velocity at time $t\\ge 0$ is given by $v(t)=\\operatorname{sec}⁡(t)\\operatorname{tan}⁡(t).$ At time $t=0$ the particle is located at the position $x=3.$ \nFind the position of the particle at time $t=\\frac{\\pi }{3}.$ Do not round the answer.\n\nThe position of the particle at $t=\\frac{\\pi }{3}$ is $x=$\n{{field-1}}." 13194139534502 true] [17592186292202 1113 #uuid "6c22f5c7-8e2f-57c6-9f32-c32dfce8fdb7" 13194139534502 true] [17592186292202 1145 "The position of the particle at $t=\\frac{\\pi }{3}$ is equal to its position at $t=0$ plus the total displacement over $t\\in [0,\\frac{\\pi }{3}].$ Therefore, we can calculate it as follows:\n\n$$\nx(\\frac{\\pi }{3})=x(0)+{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /3}v(t)\\,\\text{d}t\n$$\n\nCarrying out the computations, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(\\frac{\\pi }{3}) & =3+{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /3}\\operatorname{sec}⁡(t)\\operatorname{tan}⁡(t)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =3+{[\\operatorname{sec}⁡(t)]}_{0}^{\\pi /3} \\\\  & =3+\\operatorname{sec}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{3})-\\operatorname{sec}⁡(0) \\\\  & =3+2-1 \\\\  & =4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the position of the particle at $t=\\frac{\\pi }{3}$ is $x=4.$" 13194139534502 true] [17592186292203 1000 #edb/ref 17592186292204 13194139534502 true] [17592186292203 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139534502 true] [17592186292203 1041 "field-1" 13194139534502 true] [17592186292203 1104 #edb/ref 17592186292204 13194139534502 true] [17592186292203 1110 #uuid "80abbd92-009c-502c-86f0-4e5acd35fb54" 13194139534502 true] [17592186292204 1034 "4" 13194139534502 true] [17592186292204 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534502 true] [17592186292204 1111 #uuid "1a523402-a02c-58ca-94c8-838c42b88218" 13194139534502 true] [17592186292205 1017 #edb/ref 17592186292206 13194139534502 true] [17592186292205 1089 "q-351479" 13194139534502 true] [17592186292205 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139534502 true] [17592186292205 1100 "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14014400/assets/4c50effa85cc82dfc22a65f3792780a99b2876b77de173993b43dead23b0c1d7.png)\n\nThe graph above shows the velocity of an object moving in a straight line along the $x$-axis. At time $t=0,$ the particle is located at the position $x=-4.$ What is the position of the particle at time $t=6?$\n\nThe position of the particle at $t=6$ is $x=$\n{{field-1}}." 13194139534502 true] [17592186292205 1113 #uuid "d8794558-968e-5ecd-93b4-65457650283b" 13194139534502 true] [17592186292205 1145 "The position of the particle at $t=6$ is equal to its position at $t=0$ plus the total displacement over $t\\in [0,6].$ Therefore, we can calculate it as follows:\n\n$$\nx(6)=x(0)+{\\int }_{0}^{6}v(t)\\,\\text{d}t\n$$\n\nWe are told that $x(0)=-4$, and we can compute the integral ${\\int }_{0}^{6}v(t)\\,\\text{d}t$ by finding the signed area under the graph from $t=0$ to $t=6.$ Computing the signed area, we get\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{0}^{6}v(t)\\,\\text{d}t=10.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\nx(6)=-4+10=6.\n$$\n\nSo the position of the particle at $t=6$ is $x=6.$" 13194139534502 true] [17592186292206 1000 #edb/ref 17592186292207 13194139534502 true] [17592186292206 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139534502 true] [17592186292206 1041 "field-1" 13194139534502 true] [17592186292206 1104 #edb/ref 17592186292207 13194139534502 true] [17592186292206 1110 #uuid "c97e55e1-83e4-5b1f-87bb-5fca19f7d550" 13194139534502 true] [17592186292207 1034 "6" 13194139534502 true] [17592186292207 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534502 true] [17592186292207 1111 #uuid "223f4a43-6417-5d6b-ba39-d6f634131c7a" 13194139534502 true] [17592186292208 1017 #edb/ref 17592186292209 13194139534502 true] [17592186292208 1089 "q-351500" 13194139534502 true] [17592186292208 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045464 13194139534502 true] [17592186292208 1100 "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14014400/assets/4245a22d62605e68022fc2f02358f8f900e5370a02c04c973d0ea359249f62b6.png)\n\nThe graph above shows the velocity of an object moving in a straight line along the $x$-axis. At time $t=0,$ the particle is located at the position $x=4.$ What is the position of the particle at time $t=4?$\n\nThe position of the particle at $t=4$ is $x=$\n{{field-1}}." 13194139534502 true] [17592186292208 1113 #uuid "43c09f96-3c8c-5786-ba4e-2b3a4e2251a3" 13194139534502 true] [17592186292208 1145 "The position of the particle at $t=4$ is equal to its position at $t=0$ plus the total displacement over $t\\in [0,4].$ Therefore, we can calculate it as follows:\n\n$$\nx(4)=x(0)+{\\int }_{0}^{4}v(t)\\,\\text{d}t\n$$\n\nWe are told that $x(0)=4$, and we can compute the integral ${\\int }_{0}^{4}v(t)\\,\\text{d}t$ by finding the signed area under the graph from $t=0$ to $t=4.$ Computing the signed area, we get\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{0}^{4}v(t)\\,\\text{d}t=-1.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\nx(4)=4+(-1)=3.\n$$\n\nSo the position of the particle at $t=4$ is $x=3.$" 13194139534502 true] [17592186292209 1000 #edb/ref 17592186292210 13194139534502 true] [17592186292209 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139534502 true] [17592186292209 1041 "field-1" 13194139534502 true] [17592186292209 1104 #edb/ref 17592186292210 13194139534502 true] [17592186292209 1110 #uuid "5f2154d2-aa53-5a7e-8fd0-63167567795b" 13194139534502 true] [17592186292210 1034 "3" 13194139534502 true] [17592186292210 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534502 true] [17592186292210 1111 #uuid "94c3dfa6-d744-563e-8870-7a4c45e49b76" 13194139534502 true] [17592186292211 1017 #edb/ref 17592186292212 13194139534502 true] [17592186292211 1089 "q-351502" 13194139534502 true] [17592186292211 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045464 13194139534502 true] [17592186292211 1100 "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14014400/assets/005c8cf386537414fb0504fa26095f54fbeeaa0f88941bef41fffaf75f791ed3.png)\n\nThe graph above shows the velocity of an object moving in a straight line along the $x$-axis. At time $t=2,$ the particle is located at the position $x=8.$ What is the position of the particle at time $t=7?$\n\nThe position of the particle at $t=7$ is $x=$\n{{field-1}}." 13194139534502 true] [17592186292211 1113 #uuid "55b41cfa-7d43-5343-98ee-d2393e32d6b8" 13194139534502 true] [17592186292211 1145 "The position of the particle at $t=7$ is equal to its position at $t=2$ plus the total displacement over $t\\in [2,7].$ Therefore, we can calculate it as follows:\n\n$$\nx(7)=x(2)+{\\int }_{2}^{7}v(t)\\,\\text{d}t\n$$\n\nWe are told that $x(2)=8$, and we can compute the integral ${\\int }_{2}^{7}v(t)\\,\\text{d}t$ by finding the signed area under the graph from $t=2$ to $t=7.$ Computing the signed area, we get\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{2}^{7}v(t)\\,\\text{d}t=-3.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\nx(7)=8+(-3)=5.\n$$\n\nSo the position of the particle at $t=7$ is $x=5.$" 13194139534502 true] [17592186292212 1000 #edb/ref 17592186292213 13194139534502 true] [17592186292212 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139534502 true] [17592186292212 1041 "field-1" 13194139534502 true] [17592186292212 1104 #edb/ref 17592186292213 13194139534502 true] [17592186292212 1110 #uuid "7039c3d1-bba1-5467-98bc-f366bc511544" 13194139534502 true] [17592186292213 1034 "5" 13194139534502 true] [17592186292213 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534502 true] [17592186292213 1111 #uuid "8c7a87d3-b68d-5195-83e7-152409780892" 13194139534502 true] [17592186292214 1017 #edb/ref 17592186292215 13194139534502 true] [17592186292214 1089 "q-81506" 13194139534502 true] [17592186292214 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045464 13194139534502 true] [17592186292214 1100 "A particle $P$ moves along the $x$-axis and its velocity at time $t\\ge 0$ is given by $v(t)=\\operatorname{cos}⁡(t-\\frac{\\pi }{6}).$ At time $t=0$ the particle is located at the position $x=3.$ What is the position of the particle at time $t=\\frac{\\pi }{6}?$" 13194139534502 true] [17592186292214 1113 #uuid "1394edaf-31dd-59b4-a755-2b8323ac548f" 13194139534502 true] [17592186292214 1145 "The position of the particle at $t=\\frac{\\pi }{6}$ is equal to its position at $t=0$ plus the total displacement over $t\\in [0,\\frac{\\pi }{6}].$ Therefore, we can calculate it as follows:\n\n$$\nx(\\frac{\\pi }{6})=x(0)+{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /6}v(t)\\,\\text{d}t\n$$\n\nCarrying out the computations, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(\\frac{\\pi }{6}) & =\\frac{7}{2}+{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /6}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(t-\\frac{\\pi }{6})\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =3+{[\\operatorname{sin}⁡(t-\\frac{\\pi }{6})]}_{0}^{\\pi /6} \\\\  & =3+([\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{6}-\\frac{\\pi }{6})]-[\\operatorname{sin}⁡(0-\\frac{\\pi }{6})]) \\\\  & =3+(\\operatorname{sin}⁡(0)-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(-\\frac{\\pi }{6})) \\\\  & =3+(0-(-\\frac{1}{2})) \\\\  & =3+\\frac{1}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{7}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo the position of the particle at $t=\\frac{\\pi }{6}$ is $x=\\frac{7}{2}.$" 13194139534502 true] [17592186292215 1000 #edb/ref 17592186292216 13194139534502 true] [17592186292215 1000 #edb/ref 17592186292217 13194139534502 true] [17592186292215 1000 #edb/ref 17592186292218 13194139534502 true] [17592186292215 1000 #edb/ref 17592186292219 13194139534502 true] [17592186292215 1000 #edb/ref 17592186292220 13194139534502 true] [17592186292215 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534502 true] [17592186292215 1041 "selection" 13194139534502 true] [17592186292215 1104 #edb/ref 17592186292216 13194139534502 true] [17592186292215 1110 #uuid "8c76b68b-b8cf-58ee-b229-494f9f0c8abc" 13194139534502 true] [17592186292216 1034 "\\frac{7}{2}" 13194139534502 true] [17592186292216 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534502 true] [17592186292216 1111 #uuid "0270f788-1cdb-528c-85e3-c5e8dda56681" 13194139534502 true] [1